/collapse", "x": 0.34614531746618377, "y": 0.8475173716281225, "width": 0.2682097044060235, "height": 0.017132879592345766, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "-", "x": 0.34614531746618377, "width": 0.006188725901934561, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "Loss", "x": 0.356607691222223, "width": 0.036265530611010684, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "of", "x": 0.39714686968733837, "width": 0.01695348040236795, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "consciousness/collapse", "x": 0.41837399794381097, "width": 0.19598102392839625, "confidence": 1}]}]}, {"text": "and/or convulsions", "lines": [{"text": "and/or convulsions", "x": 0.35469261317439305, "y": 0.8700808894273598, "width": 0.16052385784073278, "height": 0.0171328795923459, "confidence": 1, "words": [{"text": "and/or", "x": 0.35469261317439305, "width": 0.05684757994610904, "confidence": 1}, {"text": "convulsions", "x": 0.4158138409746068, "width": 0.09940263004051907, "confidence": 1}]}]}]}}}, {"number": 3, "text": "Text C\n\n\n\n\n         Snakebite Management Flowchart", "extraction": "text"}, {"number": 4, "text": "Text D\n\n\n\nGiving Antivenom\n\n  • Antivenom is indicated in all children where there is evidence of envenomation.\n  • Giving antivenom should occur in consultation with a clinical toxicologist.\n  • Dilute one vial in 100mls of 0.9% saline and give IV over 15-30 min.\n  • If the child is in cardiac arrest and this is thought to be due to envenomation, then give undiluted\n    antivenom via rapid IV push.\n  • There is no weight based calculation for antivenom (the snake delivers the same amount of venom\n    regardless of the size of the child). One vial of antivenom is enough to neutralise the venom that can be\n    delivered by one snake. Clinical recovery takes time after antivenom administration and multiple vials do\n    not speed recovery.\n\nAt discharge, ensure that the family is given advice on how to recognise serum sickness:\n\n\n  • Occurs in about 30% of children given antivenom.\n  • Tends to occur 4 – 14 days following antivenom administration.\n  • Consists of flu-like symptoms, fever, myalgia, arthralgia and rash.\n  • A letter should also be written to the child’s GP regarding this.", "extraction": "text"}]}